    yearRange: "1990-1995",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM603 utilizes an incredibly robust, heavy-duty double-roller timing chain that essentially lasts the lifetime of the engine block. Unlike modern single-row chains, this unit rarely stretches. The only critical maintenance item is the hydraulic chain tensioner, which should be replaced preventatively around 250,000 km to ensure proper tension is maintained and the plastic chain guide rails do not fracture.",
    injectionType: "Indirect Injection (IDI) with a Bosch Mechanical Inline Injection Pump (M-Pump). This California/USA variant features slightly modified injection timing to meet stringent CARB emissions standards, dropping power slightly to 143 hp. The mechanical system is legendary for its durability, but the rubber fuel return lines frequently degrade and leak.",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 1 000 000+ km. While the core block is as indestructible as the European variants, the lifespan of these specific California-market engines was historically cut short by a catastrophic emissions add-on: the 'Trap Oxidizer'. This early, primitive catalytic converter was located directly in the exhaust manifold. It would routinely clog with soot, overheat, and disintegrate, sending metal shrapnel directly into the turbocharger, destroying it instantly.",
    turboType: "Single KKK or Garrett turbocharger. Like the European version, it is a robust journal-bearing turbo. However, on early models, it was frequently destroyed by the Trap Oxidizer sending debris into the turbine wheel. If the Trap Oxidizer recall was performed (replacing it with a straight pipe and a lower catalyst), the turbocharger is highly reliable.",
    ecuType: "Mechanical / Vacuum Controlled with EDS (Electronic Diesel System). To meet California emissions, this engine features a slightly more complex EDS controller that manages the EGR valve and the Trap Oxidizer regeneration cycle (if still equipped). While more complicated than the European version, it still relies primarily on vacuum pneumatics rather than modern digital CAN-bus electronics.",
    euroStandard: "US EPA / CARB Tier 1",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are incredibly robust. However, modifying this specific California variant is heavily restricted by local smog laws. Off-road builds removing the emissions equipment and installing larger injection pump elements can easily achieve massive power figures.",
