    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM612 utilizes a highly durable duplex timing chain that is massively over-engineered. It rarely stretches and is generally considered a lifetime component under normal service intervals. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 250,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap against the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI). Operating at 1350 bar, the Bosch CDI system provides microscopic fuel atomization for massive torque and excellent fuel economy. However, this engine is incredibly susceptible to the infamous 'Black Death'. The copper sealing washers underneath the fuel injectors degrade over time, allowing combustion gases to escape. This bakes diesel fuel into a solid, tar-like carbon mass that engulfs the injectors and wiring harness if not caught and repaired early.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. The cast-iron block and aluminum cylinder head are exceptionally strong. Because this fleet version is software-restricted to 163 hp, the internal mechanical and thermal stresses are marginally lower, theoretically prolonging block life. The engine's lifespan remains entirely dictated by the maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the prevention of 'Black Death', and ensuring the plastic intake manifold swirl flaps do not break.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The vacuum-actuated variable geometry turbo effectively eliminates turbo lag, providing a thick wave of 370 Nm of torque very low in the RPM range. The variable vanes are highly prone to seizing with carbon soot if the car is exclusively driven gently in city traffic, leading to underboost conditions and severe Limp Mode.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC15C6. This highly advanced engine control unit precisely manages the common-rail pressure, injector pulse width, and VGT turbocharger vanes. In this specific variant, the EDC15 utilizes a custom software map designed to restrict peak horsepower to 163 hp to satisfy fleet and taxation brackets in markets like Belgium, without compromising peak torque. The EDC15 is a favorite in the tuning community due to its accessibility and ability to be safely remapped.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "250+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The primary limitations to increasing power are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger and the fueling limits of the factory CDI injectors. With an upgraded turbo and a Stage 2 tune, the detuned OM612 becomes a highly capable performance diesel.",
