      "Transmission Vacuum Modulator Failure: The automatic transmission shifts based entirely on engine vacuum. A failed Vacuum Control Valve or cracked line will cause violent, neck-snapping shifts that will quickly destroy the transmission's internal clutch packs.",
      "Catastrophic Glow Plug Extraction Costs: While the engine is immortal, a snapped glow plug turns a minor maintenance item into a massive machining job, as the head must be removed.",
      "Cooling System Neglect: Severe overheating caused by a failed water pump, dead viscous fan clutch, or ignored radiator leaks will warp the aluminum cylinder head and blow the head gasket.",
