    "compression": "9.5:1",
    "yearRange": "2000-2002",
    "timingType": "Double overhead camshaft, 4-valve-per-cylinder, chain-driven inline-four timing layout. This fleet-calibrated M111.957 uses the same facelift-era EVO Kompressor base as the regular 163 hp version, but with a softer software tune focused on smoother delivery, lower fleet stress, and lower operating intensity. It feels calmer, less urgent, and more subdued in the mid-range than the full-output version. In healthy condition, it still feels refined, quiet, and entirely adequate for relaxed executive-car use.",
    "injectionType": "Electronically controlled multi-point fuel injection with updated ME engine management working together with mechanical supercharging. In this detuned fleet form, the system keeps the same basic strengths as the standard EVO Kompressor setup: good cold-start behavior, tidy part-throttle manners, and a more modern feel than the earlier HFM Kompressor engines. It still depends heavily on correct air-path sealing, healthy sensors, good ignition quality, and stable throttle-body behavior.",
    "engineLifespan": "320,000 to 450,000 km. The softer fleet tune does not change the basic durability of the M111 EVO architecture, and if anything it slightly reduces the everyday mechanical stress compared with the full-output version. Real ownership quality still depends far more on intake integrity, throttle-body behavior, ignition condition, supercharger-drive health, cooling-system stability, engine mounts, and the standard of previous maintenance. A properly sorted example can remain a smooth and durable long-term drivetrain.",
    "turboType": "Mechanically supercharged inline-four petrol engine using a belt-driven compressor rather than an exhaust-driven turbocharger. That still gives the engine a clean and immediate response, but in this fleet calibration the delivery is more restrained and more comfort-oriented than the regular 163 hp version. It suits quiet, low-stress driving better than enthusiastic use. A healthy example feels smooth and composed rather than quick.",
    "ecuType": "Mercedes ME engine management with electronic throttle control, adaptive fueling, ignition coordination, and supercharged calibration logic. In fleet tune, this system aims for consistency and smoothness rather than stronger headline output, but the same weaknesses still apply when sensors drift or throttle adaptation becomes unstable. A sorted car feels neat and polished. A neglected one feels flat, inconsistent, and older than it should.",
    "euroStandard": "Market-dependent catalytic petrol configuration",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "195-210 hp. The mechanical base remains the same strong M111 EVO Kompressor platform, so this fleet version still has substantial headroom relative to its softer factory calibration. In practice, restoring the engine to a perfect baseline is still more important than modifying it. This is best understood as a detuned version of a stronger package rather than a fundamentally different engine.",
