    yearRange: "1999-2002",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM611 utilizes a highly durable duplex timing chain that is massively over-engineered for the 4-cylinder block. It rarely stretches and is generally considered a lifetime component under normal service intervals. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 250,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap against the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI). This modernized facelift variant operates at an increased 1350 bar with revised injector nozzles for better atomization and power. While more refined, it remains incredibly susceptible to the infamous 'Black Death'. The copper sealing washers underneath the fuel injectors degrade over time, allowing combustion gases to escape. This bakes diesel fuel into a solid, tar-like carbon mass that engulfs the injectors and wiring harness if not caught and repaired early.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. The cast-iron block and aluminum cylinder head are exceptionally strong. The mechanical internals will effortlessly outlast the vehicle. The engine's lifespan is entirely dictated by the maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the prevention of 'Black Death', and ensuring the plastic intake manifold swirl flaps do not break and fall into the combustion chamber.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The vacuum-actuated variable geometry turbo in this facelift version is mapped for higher boost, effectively eliminating turbo lag and providing 315 Nm of torque very low in the RPM range. The variable vanes are highly prone to seizing with carbon soot if the car is exclusively driven gently in city traffic, leading to underboost conditions and severe Limp Mode.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC15C6. This highly advanced engine control unit precisely manages the common-rail pressure, injector pulse width, and VGT turbocharger vanes. The EDC15 is a favorite in the tuning community due to its accessibility and ability to be safely remapped for significant torque gains. Fortunately, the facelift W210 era completely resolved the bio-degradable wiring harness catastrophe of earlier models.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "220+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The primary limitations to increasing power are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger and the fueling limits of the factory CDI injectors. With a Stage 1 tune, the 143 hp OM611 becomes an incredibly lively and capable performer.",
