      "Lethal Chassis Corrosion (W210): The engine is a masterpiece, but it is bolted into a highly vulnerable chassis. Severe structural rust in the front spring perches, subframes, and jacking points will render the car unsafe to drive long before the engine dies.",
      "Financial Ruin via Black Death: If an injector is left leaking for too long, the baked carbon essentially welds the injector into the cylinder head. Removing it often requires a hydraulic puller, and in severe cases, the cylinder head must be replaced.",
      "Engine Ingestion of Swirl Flaps: A broken plastic swirl flap entering the combustion chamber will instantly destroy the piston, valves, and potentially the turbocharger on its way out.",
      "722.6 Conductor Plate Failure: The 5-speed automatic transmission will drop into Limp Mode and refuse to shift if the internal conductor plate fails due to neglected fluid changes.",
