    yearRange: "1998-2002",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM611 utilizes a highly durable duplex timing chain. In this severely detuned taxi variant, the mechanical stress on the chain is practically non-existent. It is a true lifetime component that will never stretch under normal use. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 300,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI). Operating at 1350 bar, the Bosch CDI system provides excellent fuel economy. This specific taxi version features a highly conservative fueling map designed specifically to protect the early CDI injectors from premature wear during endless hours of city idling. Despite the detune, it remains incredibly susceptible to the infamous 'Black Death'. The copper sealing washers underneath the fuel injectors degrade over time, allowing combustion gases to escape and bake diesel fuel into a solid carbon mass.",
    engineLifespan: "600 000 - 1 000 000+ km. Because this fleet version is software-restricted to just 115 hp, the internal mechanical and thermal stresses are extraordinarily low. The cast-iron block and aluminum cylinder head are practically immortal under these conditions. The engine's lifespan is entirely dictated by the maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the prevention of 'Black Death', and ensuring the plastic intake manifold swirl flaps do not break.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The vacuum-actuated variable geometry turbo is mapped very conservatively on this model to limit peak boost pressures. The variable vanes are highly prone to seizing with carbon soot, especially since taxi driving involves endless low-speed urban crawling that prevents the exhaust from getting hot enough to clear the soot.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC15C0 / EDC15C6. This engine control unit precisely manages the common-rail system, but utilizes a custom software map designed to artificially restrict peak horsepower to 115 hp. This was specifically requested by fleet operators to maximize engine longevity and protect the drivetrain from aggressive taxi drivers. The EDC15 is a favorite in the tuning community due to its ability to be safely remapped back to standard output.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 2 / Euro 3",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "200+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The 115 hp limit is purely artificial. With a standard Stage 1 tune, the detuned taxi variant safely jumps back up to 160+ horsepower without compromising block integrity.",
