    yearRange: "1996-1997",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M119 utilizes an incredibly robust double-row timing chain that is virtually immune to stretching under normal use. However, the upper timing chain guide rails are constructed from plastic that becomes dangerously brittle from decades of extreme V8 heat cycles. If these guide rails fracture, the broken plastic debris will drop into the timing cover and jam the chain sprocket, causing immediate, catastrophic valve-to-piston contact. Preventative replacement of these upper plastic guides every 150,000 km is absolutely mandatory to save the engine block.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection via Bosch ME-SFI (Motor Electronics). This system utilizes a hot-wire mass airflow sensor to accurately meter incoming air. The injection system is highly reliable and provides excellent fuel atomization. However, early W210 models still suffered from the infamous bio-degradable eco-wiring harness issue. The insulation on the engine harness will crumble to dust, causing severe electrical shorts that can destroy the electronic throttle body and the engine control module.",
    engineLifespan: "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The M119 engine block is legendary for its endurance, featuring a closed-deck aluminum block with Alusil cylinder coatings. While the physical block is nearly indestructible, the engine's lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to combat severe oil leaks, replace the crumbling eco-wiring harness, and preemptively replace the timing chain guides.",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. The M119 relies entirely on its 4.2-liter displacement and advanced 32-valve, four-camshaft breathing capability to generate immense, immediate torque. The throttle response is extremely sharp and completely linear, delivering a pure, unfiltered V8 power delivery.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME-SFI. The ECU manages fueling, ignition, and the electronic throttle actuator perfectly. These modules are very expensive to replace if they are short-circuited by a crumbling eco-wiring harness. Aftermarket tuning offers slight gains but is rarely cost-effective compared to larger displacement models.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 2",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp. The internal components, including forged connecting rods and an internally balanced crankshaft, are over-engineered to extreme degrees. While the block can technically handle forced induction, it is highly unusual to turbocharge or supercharge the 4.2L variant due to the complexity and cost.",
