    yearRange: "1997-2002",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M112 V6 utilizes a highly durable double-row timing chain that is incredibly robust. Unlike older V8 architectures, the M112 is not known for catastrophic plastic guide rail failures, though high-mileage examples should be inspected for general chain slack. A slight rattle on cold start may indicate a failing hydraulic tensioner, which should be replaced preventatively to protect the valvetrain.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). The Bosch ME system is highly advanced, extremely reliable, and provides perfect fueling mapping. Crucially, the M112 completely escapes the devastating bio-degradable eco-wiring harness catastrophe of the mid-1990s inline-6 engines. The fuel injectors are standard electronic units that rarely fail, provided the fuel filter is changed regularly.",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 500 000+ miles. The M112 is widely considered one of the most reliable and bulletproof V6 engines ever built by Mercedes-Benz. The aluminum block utilizes incredibly tough Silitec (Alusil) cylinder linings that show practically zero wear even after massive American highway mileages. By utilizing a simpler 18-valve (3 valves per cylinder) design with a single overhead cam per bank, engineers dramatically reduced mechanical complexity and increased the engine's lifespan.",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. The M112 relies entirely on its 3.2-liter displacement to generate a smooth wave of 310 Nm of torque. This provides a muscular, instant throttle response that perfectly suits American interstates, delivering effortless cruising capability without the thermal complexity of a turbocharger.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME-SFI 2.0 / 2.8. The ME system manages the fueling, ignition, and electronic throttle perfectly. This specific USA variant features a unique software calibration and stricter evaporative emissions systems designed to meet stringent EPA standards. The engine utilizes a twin-spark ignition system (two spark plugs per cylinder) to maximize combustion efficiency.",
    euroStandard: "US EPA / CARB Tier 1",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "400+ hp. The forged internals of the M112 engine are exceptionally strong. This engine architecture is heavily related to the supercharged AMG V6 found in the C32 AMG. Bolting an aftermarket supercharger (like a Kleemann kit) to a naturally aspirated E 320 safely pushes it past 330 horsepower without opening the block.",
