    timingType: "Simplex roller chain. The OM642 utilizes a single-row timing chain. Unlike the immortal double-row chains of previous inline-six diesels, this chain is highly prone to stretching at higher mileages (usually beyond 250,000 km). Preventative replacement of the hydraulic chain tensioner can prolong its life, but a stretched chain will eventually require a significant replacement job to avoid jumping teeth and catastrophic engine damage.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) utilizing Bosch piezo-electric injectors operating at up to 1600 bar. This extremely high pressure ensures microscopic fuel atomization for maximum torque and lower emissions. While slightly more robust against 'Black Death' than older engines, the Piezo injectors themselves are incredibly expensive to replace if they fail electronically or suffer from poor spray patterns.",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The aluminum block with cast-iron cylinder liners is structurally incredibly robust. However, the true lifespan of the engine is almost entirely dictated by the maintenance of its complex peripheral systems. If the oil cooler seals leak and are ignored, or if the DPF system clogs and causes excessive exhaust backpressure, the repair bills will outpace the car's value.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT) mounted in the valley of the V6 engine. It provides incredibly fast spool times and eliminates turbo lag, delivering peak torque from just 1,600 RPM. The electronic turbo actuator is prone to failure from extreme heat cycling, and the turbo intake seal is notorious for leaking oil directly onto the swirl flap motor.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16CP31. A highly sophisticated engine control unit managing the Piezo injectors, VGT turbocharger, and the exhaust aftertreatment system. It provides extensive diagnostic capabilities and is highly responsive to aftermarket tuning, capable of unleashing massive torque gains, though the DPF limits extreme thermal tuning.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and crankshaft are immensely strong. The primary limitations for tuning are the high-pressure fuel pump (CP3) capacity, the stock turbocharger's airflow limit, and the strict thermal constraints of the DPF system.",
