    yearRange: "2004-2005",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM648 utilizes a massive duplex timing chain that is incredibly robust. Because this E 280 CDI is a software-detuned version of the 3.2L engine, the mechanical stress is remarkably low, meaning the chain essentially never stretches under normal maintenance. It provides bulletproof reliability for the valvetrain. The only recommended maintenance is the replacement of the hydraulic chain tensioner at very high mileages (250,000+ km) to ensure the plastic guide rails are not battered by a loose chain on cold starts.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI). Operating at 1600 bar, the Bosch CDI system provides excellent fuel atomization. However, this system suffers from the dreaded 'Black Death'. The copper sealing washers at the base of the injectors fail, allowing combustion gases to escape and bake diesel fuel into a rock-hard carbon tar that coats the cylinder head and destroys the wiring. Preventative replacement of these copper seals is absolutely mandatory.",
    engineLifespan: "500 000 - 1 000 000+ km. The core of the OM648 is a phenomenally strong cast-iron block that is highly resistant to wear. As this is the detuned 177 hp version of the 3.2L block, it operates in a perpetual state of mechanical ease. The physical block will run virtually forever, but the lifespan of the car is heavily dictated by the maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the intake swirl flaps, and the infamous Sensotronic (SBC) brake system of the pre-facelift era.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The OM648 uses a sophisticated electronic-actuated variable geometry turbo. Because the torque is limited to 425 Nm by software, the turbo is rarely pushed to its thermal limits. The VNT vanes are prone to seizing with carbon soot if the car is exclusively driven gently in city traffic, leading to underboost conditions and Limp Mode.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C2. A highly advanced and tunable engine control unit that precisely manages the common rail system. In this model, the ECU holds the artificial software restriction that limits output to 177 hp (down from 204 hp in the E 320 CDI). The EDC16 is legendary in the tuning community because it is highly accessible and easily unlocked.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3 / Euro 4 (Depending on DPF option)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are identically strong to the E 320 CDI. The primary limitations to increasing power are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger, the fueling limits of the factory CDI injectors, and the torque capacity of the 722.6 automatic transmission. Removing the software restriction instantly yields 204+ hp safely.",
