    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM646 EVO relies on a heavy-duty duplex timing chain that is practically immortal. It completely avoids the severe stretching issues that ruined the reputation of its OM651 successor. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 250,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap against the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) utilizing Delphi piezo-electric/solenoid injectors operating at 1600 bar. This system delivers highly refined atomization for smooth idling and excellent efficiency. However, the Delphi injectors are notably more sensitive to fuel contamination than older Bosch units. The infamous 'Black Death' (failing copper injector seals) remains a severe threat, baking raw diesel into solid carbon on the cylinder head if ignored.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. Because this fleet version is artificially restricted to 163 hp, the internal mechanical and thermal stresses on the cast-iron block are practically non-existent. The physical engine will outlast the car. The true lifespan is dictated entirely by preventative maintenance of the Delphi injectors, the DPF system, and the fragile plastic intake manifold swirl flaps.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The electronically actuated variable geometry turbo eliminates lag and provides the full 400 Nm of torque incredibly early in the rev range. The electronic actuator is prone to failure from extreme engine bay heat, and the VNT vanes can seize with carbon soot if the car is primarily driven in stop-and-go city traffic.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C31. This highly advanced ECU manages the common-rail pressure, VGT turbo, and DPF regeneration. In this variant, the software explicitly restricts peak horsepower to 163 hp to satisfy Belgian taxation and fleet economy standards, while leaving the 400 Nm torque output intact. It is highly responsive to stage 1 tuning, which safely removes this artificial restriction.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 (with Diesel Particulate Filter)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The primary limitations are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger, the strict exhaust backpressure limits of the DPF, and the flow limits of the Delphi injectors. Removing the software restriction instantly yields massive gains.",
