    yearRange: "2006-2009",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM646 EVO features an incredibly robust duplex timing chain architecture. Unlike the OM651 engine that replaced it, this chain is located at the front of the engine and is essentially immune to stretching under normal use. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 250,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap against the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) utilizing Delphi piezo-electric injectors operating at up to 1600 bar. This system provides superior fuel atomization for a remarkably smooth idle and excellent power delivery. However, the Delphi injectors are notorious for being highly sensitive to poor fuel quality and can fail internally. Furthermore, the engine is susceptible to 'Black Death', where failing copper injector washers allow combustion gases to bake raw diesel into a solid carbon block across the cylinder head.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. The cast-iron block and forged rotating assembly are virtually indestructible. As the 170 hp variant, it operates under very manageable stress levels. The physical block will effortlessly outlast the W211 chassis. The engine's true lifespan is dictated entirely by preventative maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the DPF, and deleting the fragile plastic intake manifold swirl flaps before they break and are ingested.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The electronically actuated variable geometry turbo eliminates lag and provides the full 400 Nm of torque almost instantly. The electronic actuator is prone to failure from extreme engine bay heat, and the VNT vanes can seize with carbon soot if the car is strictly driven gently in urban environments.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C31. A highly sophisticated ECU managing the Delphi common-rail system, VGT turbo, and complex DPF regeneration cycles. The EDC16 is legendary in the tuning community because it is highly accessible and responds incredibly well to software remaps, safely unlocking massive torque gains while maintaining reliability.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 4 (with Diesel Particulate Filter)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "260+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The primary limitations to increasing power are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger, the strict exhaust backpressure limits of the factory DPF, and the flow limits of the Delphi injectors. With a Stage 1 tune, the 170 hp OM646 EVO easily pushes past 200 hp safely.",
