    yearRange: "2002-2005",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM647 uses a highly durable duplex timing chain inherited from the OM612. It is massively over-engineered for the 5-cylinder block and rarely stretches. It is a lifetime component under normal service intervals. The hydraulic chain tensioner is the only preventative maintenance item, recommended for replacement around 250,000 km to prevent cold-start chain slap against the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI). Operating at 1600 bar, the Bosch CDI system provides excellent fuel atomization. However, this system suffers terribly from the dreaded 'Black Death'. The copper sealing washers at the base of the injectors fail constantly, allowing combustion gases to escape and bake diesel fuel into a rock-hard carbon tar that coats the cylinder head and destroys the wiring. Preventative replacement of these copper seals is absolutely mandatory.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. The core of the OM647 is a phenomenally strong cast-iron block that is highly resistant to wear. The physical block will run virtually forever, but the lifespan of the car is heavily dictated by the maintenance of the high-pressure fuel system, the fragile intake swirl flaps, and the infamous Sensotronic (SBC) brake system of the pre-facelift era.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT) / Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). The OM647 uses a sophisticated electronic-actuated variable geometry turbo that eliminates lag. The VNT vanes are highly prone to seizing with carbon soot if the car is exclusively driven gently in city traffic, leading to underboost conditions and Limp Mode.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C2. A highly advanced and tunable engine control unit that precisely manages the common rail system. The EDC16 is legendary in the tuning community because it is highly accessible and easily unlocked for massive mid-range torque improvements.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3 (Euro 4 with optional DPF)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and pistons are immensely strong. The primary limitations to increasing power are the thermal capacity of the stock turbocharger and the torque capacity of the 722.6 automatic transmission. Upgrading the turbo and nozzles allows the 5-cylinder block to safely exceed 240+ hp.",
