    "yearRange": "2004-2006",
    "timingType": "Double overhead camshaft, 4-valve-per-cylinder, chain-driven supercharged inline-four timing layout. The M271.941 in the E 200 NGT BlueEFFICIENCY combines standard Kompressor architecture with factory bi-fuel petrol and CNG capability. It feels broadly similar to a regular E 200 Kompressor, but the dual-fuel system adds complexity and makes condition and diagnostics more important than on a normal petrol-only car.",
    "injectionType": "Electronically controlled manifold injection with factory-integrated bi-fuel petrol/CNG operation, airflow metering, and supercharger load coordination. The system was designed as a proper Mercedes production solution rather than a simple aftermarket gas conversion. When the ignition, fuel switching, pressure regulation, and intake baseline are all healthy, it feels much more cohesive than most converted CNG cars.",
    "engineLifespan": "220,000 to 350,000 km. The basic M271 long block can last well with disciplined oil service and proper timing-system care, but the ownership picture is broader than on a normal E 200 Kompressor because the NGT also adds gas injectors, pressure control hardware, shut-off valves, sensors, and tank-related inspection requirements. A good one can be dependable, but a neglected one gets expensive through several overlapping medium faults.",
    "turboType": "Mechanically supercharged petrol engine with factory bi-fuel CNG capability. The Kompressor setup gives the W211 acceptable low-end and mid-range response, while the CNG system focuses more on running-cost efficiency and emissions than on performance. It is best understood as a practical executive dual-fuel drivetrain rather than a sporty one.",
    "ecuType": "Factory Mercedes engine management for supercharged petrol operation with integrated petrol/CNG coordination. This gives the NGT a more OEM-like and predictable feel than many converted gas cars, but it also means fault tracing has to consider both the base engine and the gas system together. A sorted example feels clean and consistent; a neglected one can produce confusing mixed symptoms.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 4 / market-dependent configuration",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "180-195 hp. The base M271 has some modest headroom on stock internals, but on the NGT the sensible path is preserving reliability, fuel-system integrity, and smooth switching rather than chasing power gains. The real value here is the factory dual-fuel setup.",
