    yearRange: "2006-2009",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The mighty M156 relies on a robust timing chain that generally lasts the life of the engine. However, the cam phasers (adjusters) and the timing chain tensioners are known weak points. Rattle on cold startup is the definitive warning sign of bleeding tensioners or wearing cam adjusters. If ignored, the loose chain can wear down the plastic guides, leading to costly timing cover repairs and potential timing jump.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). As a naturally aspirated performance engine, it utilizes traditional port injection rather than direct injection. The US-spec calibration features slightly different fueling logic and evaporative emissions controls to pass stringent North American testing. The injection system is highly reliable, but the engine is sensitive to intake manifold leaks, where the central magnesium plate corrodes and causes vacuum leaks.",
    engineLifespan: "200 000 - 350 000+ km. The M156 is the first engine entirely designed from the ground up by AMG. The closed-deck aluminum block with LDS (twin-wire arc sprayed) cylinder coatings is incredibly strong. However, its lifespan is entirely dictated by the owner's vigilance regarding the dreaded M156 head bolt issue and valvetrain wear. If the head bolts are proactively upgraded and the lifters/cams are monitored, the block will endure massive mileage.",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. The M156 represents the pinnacle of large-displacement, high-revving N/A V8s. It utilizes a dual-length magnesium intake manifold to optimize airflow across the entire rev range. Throttle response is razor-sharp, delivering a brutal, linear swell of 630 Nm of torque accompanied by one of the greatest exhaust notes in automotive history.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7. A highly sophisticated engine control unit managing the four variable camshafts, twin throttle bodies, and fueling. The US variant features restrictive carbon traps in the airboxes (ROW - Rest of World airboxes omit these). Tuning the ME 9.7 unlocks the engine's true breathing capability and easily yields significant power gains.",
    euroStandard: "US EPA / CARB Tier 2 Bin 5 (Equivalent to Euro 4)",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "700+ hp. The forged crankshaft and robust connecting rods handle immense power. While naturally aspirated tuning maxes out around 550 hp, bolting on a positive displacement supercharger (such as a Weistec or Magnuson unit) pushes the stock bottom end past 700 horsepower with ease.",
