    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The OM646 employs a heavy-duty duplex timing chain at the front of the block. Because this specific fleet version is software-restricted to just 102 hp, the mechanical stress on this chain is virtually zero. It is exceptionally reliable and requires no scheduled maintenance beyond monitoring the hydraulic tensioner, which can be replaced at 250,000+ km to maintain perfect chain geometry.",
    injectionType: "Common-Rail Direct Injection (CDI) using Bosch solenoid injectors (up to 1600 bar). This system is known for high reliability and tolerance to fuel variations, though it remains highly prone to 'Black Death' (carbon buildup from failing copper injector washers). Regular inspection of the injector base area is strictly required to prevent carbon from hardening around the injector body.",
    engineLifespan: "600 000 - 1 000 000+ km. The cast-iron block and aluminum cylinder head are engineered for extreme-mileage taxi service. Operating at a severely detuned 102 hp, the engine practically idles its way through life. With consistent oil changes, the mechanical core easily reaches a million kilometers without needing a rebuild.",
    turboType: "Single Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). The turbocharger features electronic geometry control, ensuring immediate torque availability despite the low peak output. The VNT mechanism is durable but can become sticky with soot if the car is only driven gently in city traffic; occasional highway runs are beneficial for keeping the vanes clean.",
    ecuType: "Bosch EDC16C2. A robust engine management system that precisely controls common-rail pressure and turbo geometry. In this variant, the software explicitly limits output to 102 hp to maximize fleet longevity and fuel economy. It handles stage 1 software unlocks with absolute ease.",
