    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M113K uses an incredibly robust double-row timing chain that is widely considered indestructible. Unlike earlier and later architectures, this chain is practically a lifetime component. The only recommended maintenance is replacing the hydraulic chain tensioner at high mileages to prevent cold-start rattle.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). The M113K utilizes a highly reliable port injection system with upgraded, high-flow injectors to support the massive volume of air forced into the cylinders by the supercharger. It completely avoids the carbon-buildup issues of modern direct-injection engines.",
    engineLifespan: "400 000 - 800 000+ km. The M113K is legendary for its durability. Affectionately nicknamed the 'German 2JZ' by tuners, the closed-deck aluminum block features incredibly tough Silitec (Alusil) cylinder linings, and the rotating assembly is forged to handle the forced induction. The physical block will effortlessly outlast the chassis.",
    turboType: "IHI Lysholm Twin-Screw Supercharger. Belt-driven and nestled in the V of the engine, it delivers immediate, brutal torque with absolutely zero lag. It is paired with an air-to-water intercooler system. The factory Bosch intercooler pump is notorious for failing, causing the intake charge to overheat and the ECU to shut off the supercharger to protect the engine.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.8. A highly sophisticated and extremely tunable engine control unit. It manages the twin-spark ignition, fueling, and the supercharger's electromagnetic clutch. It responds phenomenally well to tuning, allowing for massive power gains with simple pulley swaps and software flashing.",
    euroStandard: "Euro 3 / Euro 4",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "700+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, crankshaft, and pistons are over-engineered to an absurd degree. The M113K block can handle massive increases in boost pressure. The primary limitations are fuel delivery, transmission torque capacity, and the engine's ability to cool the supercharged intake charge.",
