    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M113 engine features an incredibly robust double-row timing chain that is widely considered indestructible. Unlike later architectures, this chain is practically a lifetime component. The only recommended maintenance is replacing the hydraulic chain tensioner at high mileages to prevent cold-start rattle and protect the plastic guide rails.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). The M113 utilizes a highly reliable port injection system. It completely avoids the carbon-buildup issues on intake valves that plague modern direct-injection engines. The US-spec calibration features slightly different fueling logic and evaporative emissions controls to pass stringent North American EPA testing.",
    engineLifespan: "250 000 - 500 000+ miles. The M113 is legendary for its durability. The closed-deck aluminum block features incredibly tough Silitec (Alusil) cylinder linings. The physical engine block will effortlessly outlast the chassis. The true lifespan is dictated by the maintenance of the infamous SBC brake system and AirMatic suspension.",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. The 5.0-liter V8 provides a smooth, muscular, and instant throttle response that perfectly suits American interstates, pinning the driver to the seat from incredibly low RPMs without the complexity of forced induction.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.8. A highly sophisticated engine control unit managing the twin-spark ignition and electronic throttle. This specific USA variant features a unique software calibration designed to meet stringent EPA standards, resulting in a nominal SAE rating of 302 hp. It responds phenomenally well to tuning.",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 2",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "500+ hp. The forged connecting rods and crankshaft are over-engineered to an absurd degree. The M113 block can handle massive increases in power; bolting an aftermarket supercharger safely pushes it past 450 horsepower without opening the block.",
