    yearRange: "2006-2009",
    timingType: "Double-roller chain. The M273 transitioned to a 4-valve DOHC design. EARLY models (sold as 2007-2008 MY in the US) suffer from a catastrophic manufacturing defect: the idler gear (timing chain sprocket) was made from soft metal. The timing chain literally chews the teeth off the gear, causing severe timing faults (Codes 1200/1208), metal shavings in the oil, and eventual engine destruction. Fixing this requires removing the engine from the car. Later models (2009+) received hardened gears.",
    injectionType: "Multi-Point Sequential Fuel Injection (ME-SFI). Mercedes-Benz retained port injection for this generation, which is a massive blessing for long-term reliability. It completely avoids the severe carbon buildup on intake valves that plagues the later M278 direct-injected engines. The injection system itself is highly reliable.",
    engineLifespan: "150 000 - 250 000+ miles. If the engine falls outside the affected idler gear VIN range, or if the repair has already been performed, the M273 is a phenomenal, highly durable V8. The aluminum block with Silitec cylinder linings is robust. The lifespan is dictated by the timing chain idler gear, the intake manifold tumble flaps, and the AirMatic suspension.",
    turboType: "Naturally Aspirated. The 5.5-liter V8 breathes naturally, utilizing a complex dual-stage variable intake manifold. It provides a massive 382 horsepower (SAE) and 391 lb-ft (530 Nm) of torque, delivering acceleration that rivals early 2000s AMG models with buttery-smooth, lag-free delivery.",
    ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7. A highly advanced ECU that controls the continuous variable valve timing on all four camshafts and the variable intake manifold. The US variant features slightly different software calibration to comply with EPA standards, resulting in the 382 hp rating. Tuning the ME 9.7 can easily safely push the engine past 400 horsepower.",
    euroStandard: "US EPA Tier 2",
    maxPowerStockInternals: "550+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is strong. While it doesn't have the forged pedigree of the AMG M156, it can handle significant naturally aspirated tuning and mild forced induction.",
