    "yearRange": "2002-2005",
    "timingType": "Single overhead camshaft per cylinder bank, 3-valve-per-cylinder, double-roller-chain-driven naturally aspirated V6 timing layout. A USA-spec M112.949 delivers essentially the same classic, durable Mercedes V6 character as the global E320, but with slightly reduced output figures due to stricter emissions calibration. Even so, it still suits the W211 very well: smooth-running, relaxed on long journeys, and far more like an effortless luxury-sedan engine than a sporty one.",
    "injectionType": "Microprocessor-controlled multi-point manifold fuel injection with hot-film air-mass sensing and Bosch ME engine management, using USA federal and California-oriented emissions calibration. The design remains simpler and easier to maintain than later direct-injection or more complicated Mercedes petrol engines, which is a major reason why long-term ownership is usually favorable. In good condition it offers smooth idle quality, refined throttle response, and a torque-rich, effortless mid-range character, even if its personality is more comfort-oriented than aggressive.",
    "engineLifespan": "300,000 to 500,000 km. The key to long life in a USA-spec M112.949 is not some exotic technical trick, but simply that the base engine is strong while its common issues are mostly related to seals, vacuum lines, breather parts, cooling components, and ignition maintenance. If the engine stays dry, vacuum-tight, warms up properly, and gets regular oil changes, it can tolerate very high mileage. Bad examples usually do not fail dramatically, but instead become oily, more sluggish, and less smooth over time.",
    "turboType": "Naturally aspirated V6 petrol engine. The USA-spec E320 is not about raw acceleration, but about moving the W211 with ease, refinement, and cultured sound quality. Even with its slightly softer emissions-driven calibration, it still has more than enough strength to deliver the calm premium feel that suits the model. This engine is at its best when it works quietly, smoothly, and naturally under load.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME engine management with adaptive fueling, ignition control, hot-film air-mass measurement, and emissions-oriented USA calibration. The system is simpler and generally less problematic than later Mercedes V6 control systems, but it still reacts noticeably to vacuum leaks, breather faults, spark plug condition, and oil leaks. When everything is correct, the car feels very smooth and cohesive; when it is not, the deterioration is usually gradual rather than dramatic.",
    "euroStandard": "USA federal / California emissions-specific configuration",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "232-240 hp. On this engine, tuning is almost completely secondary because its value does not come from chasing a few extra horsepower, but from its refined running, solid torque, and durability. The best 'tuning' here is usually restoring the intake system, vacuum system, ignition system, and cooling system to near-factory condition.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "15.5-16.2 L/100km",
      "highway": "7.8-8.3 L/100km",
      "mixed": "10.8-11.4 L/100km",
      "sporty": "13.5-17.5 L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "Approx. 8.0L 5W-40 or 0W-40 fully synthetic oil meeting suitable Mercedes-Benz petrol-engine approvals. This engine especially rewards sensible, shorter oil-change intervals, because the biggest enemies of an ageing M112 are usually not internal structural weakness, but seal ageing, contamination, and delayed baseline maintenance.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Valve cover gasket seepage is common on ageing M112 engines and is often one of the first visible leak points.",
      "Front timing cover and upper-engine sealing leaks can develop with age and create an engine that looks messier than its real internal condition.",
      "Crankcase breather and ventilation-system ageing can increase oil use, worsen oil seepage, and contribute to false-air behavior.",
      "Vacuum hoses become hard and brittle with age, which can affect idle quality, fuel trims, and general smoothness.",
      "The variable intake manifold linkage and related vacuum-control hardware can wear, stick, or fail, affecting torque delivery and mixture behavior.",
      "Neglected spark plugs can shorten ignition-coil life because the M112 uses two spark plugs per cylinder.",
      "Thermostat ageing is common and can cause lazy warm-up, lower operating temperature, weaker cabin heat, and higher fuel consumption.",
      "Water pump and general cooling-system ageing should be taken seriously because old pumps, hoses, and coolant neglect reduce reliability margin.",
      "Camshaft adjuster solenoid leak issues can allow oil migration into the engine harness if ignored.",
      "Engine mounts often collapse with age and can make the otherwise smooth V6 feel harsher and more tired than it really is."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "The biggest vulnerability of the USA-spec M112.949 is that buyers hear it is a durable Mercedes V6 and then assume age-related maintenance no longer matters.",
      "Oil leaks are a real vulnerability because the basic engine often remains mechanically strong while external sealing steadily deteriorates with time.",
      "Breather and vacuum-system condition is a major vulnerability because small air leaks quietly spoil drivability without always making the engine feel obviously broken.",
      "The intake-manifold linkage and vacuum-control system are weak points because ageing here changes the engine's character long before full failure.",
      "Ignition neglect is a vulnerability because the twin-plug setup rewards proper service and punishes owners who stretch plug intervals too far.",
      "Cooling-system complacency is dangerous because thermostat drift and water-pump ageing slowly reduce reliability margin without dramatic early symptoms.",
      "Cam-adjuster solenoid oil leakage matters because it can contaminate wiring and create more expensive electrical issues if ignored.",
      "Cheap aftermarket seals, breather parts, and ignition components are a vulnerability because the engine loses its smoothness quickly when repaired badly.",
      "Weak service history is still risky, even on an M112, because simplicity does not cancel years of poor maintenance.",
      "This engine is also vulnerable to being underdiagnosed, where owners accept oil sweating, weak idle quality, or extra fuel use as normal ageing instead of addressing the real causes."
    ],
