    "oilSpecification": "Approx. 8.0L 5W-40 or 0W-40 fully synthetic oil meeting suitable Mercedes-Benz petrol-engine approvals.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Balance-shaft sprocket wear is the headline early M272 problem and remains the single biggest reason pre-facelift E350 buyers need to inspect history carefully.",
      "Timing-chain stretch and timing-correlation drift can develop alongside balance-shaft wear or as part of the same broader timing-family problem.",
      "The variable intake manifold can suffer internal flap and linkage wear, causing weaker mid-range response, fault codes, and expensive replacement decisions.",
      "Oil cooler seal leaks in the V of the engine are a classic M272 weakness and often create messy leaks that spread downward before the source is identified.",
      "Camshaft adjuster magnet and solenoid sealing leaks can create oil contamination and progressively rougher running if ignored.",
      "Thermostat and water-pump ageing are common and can make the engine run less crisply, consume more fuel, and lose some of its premium feel.",
      "Engine mounts, ignition coils, and neglected spark plugs can make the otherwise refined 3.5-liter V6 feel harsher and less expensive than it should."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "The main vulnerability of the pre-facelift M272.964 is that production-era timing risk matters more than mileage alone.",
      "Long oil intervals are especially harmful because this engine responds strongly to oil quality in both timing and cam-control behavior.",
      "Intake-manifold wear is a vulnerability because it degrades performance and smoothness before the car always feels obviously broken.",
      "Oil leak neglect is dangerous because cooler-seal and upper-engine seepage can contaminate surrounding areas and hide the real source of trouble.",
      "Cheap aftermarket timing, sealing, and intake parts can ruin the engine's premium character even when the repair initially seems successful.",
      "Weak diagnostics are a major vulnerability because timing, intake, ignition, and oil-related faults often overlap and mislead inexperienced owners.",
      "Short test drives can hide the real condition of an early M272, making a merely acceptable car feel better than it truly is."
    ],
