    "yearRange": "2006-2009",
    "timingType": "Double overhead camshaft, 4-valve-per-cylinder, chain-driven naturally aspirated V6 timing layout with continuously variable camshaft adjustment. In facelift form, the W211 E350 feels like a more complete expression of what the M272.964 was supposed to be from the beginning: strong, refined, smooth, and properly premium without needing turbocharging or V8 excess. The updated car around the engine is slightly more mature in its presentation and usability, and that helps the 3.5-liter V6 feel more integrated, less experimental, and more like a finished executive package. It still belongs to the same M272 family and still deserves careful ownership, but in facelift guise it is easier to recommend because the car tends to feel more polished and the balance-shaft story is more favorable than on the earliest examples.",
    "injectionType": "Electronically controlled multi-point fuel injection with variable intake operation, adaptive ignition calibration, continuous camshaft adjustment, and Mercedes/Bosch engine management for a naturally aspirated V6. The facelift E350 still depends on the same general formula as the earlier car, but when healthy it delivers one of the best naturally aspirated petrol experiences in the W211 range below the V8s. It feels strong from the middle of the rev range, smooth at idle, refined under load, and very relaxed at speed. Because the system relies on intake health, oil quality, good sealing, and clean control logic, the car rewards careful maintenance more than casual ownership, but when sorted it feels properly expensive in a way that many later downsized engines cannot match.",
    "engineLifespan": "240,000 to 380,000 km. The facelift M272.964 can cover high mileage very convincingly, especially when compared with the anxiety surrounding the earliest M272 years, but longevity still depends on evidence rather than assumption. Cars that receive frequent oil changes, correct cooling-system care, proper intake-manifold diagnosis, and early leak repair age much better than cars maintained only to the minimum. A good facelift E350 can remain a genuinely satisfying long-distance petrol executive car for a very long time. A lazy one usually deteriorates through refinement loss, oil leaks, thermostat laziness, and increasingly expensive medium-scale repairs rather than one dramatic engine-ending event.",
    "turboType": "Naturally aspirated V6 petrol engine. The facelift E350 offers exactly the sort of smooth and muscular petrol performance that suits a high-quality mid-2000s Mercedes executive sedan. It is fast enough to feel special, but not in a frantic or theatrical way; instead it feels calm, strong, and very mature. The engine's real appeal is the combination of quiet confidence, naturally aspirated response, and easy long-distance pace. It gives the facelift W211 the kind of balanced petrol identity that many buyers want when they are not interested in diesel or V8 ownership.",
    "ecuType": "Mercedes-Benz/Bosch engine management with adaptive fueling, knock control, variable camshaft adjustment logic, and variable intake coordination. In facelift form the M272.964 still depends on accurate diagnostics and good maintenance, but the car generally feels more settled and more coherent when everything is correct. The engine responds sharply yet smoothly, idles with real polish, and maintains a strong premium character across the rev range. Even so, faults in intake behavior, ignition quality, leak-related contamination, or neglected timing-related data can still gradually erode that character, so the best cars are always the ones with evidence of careful mechanical attention rather than cosmetic tidiness alone.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 4",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "290-300 hp. The facelift M272.964 is still not a tuning-first engine, because the smartest ownership path is preserving factory smoothness, torque delivery, and system health rather than chasing small naturally aspirated gains. A perfectly sorted stock facelift E350 is already a genuinely satisfying road car.",
